      "content": "I strongly advise against taking excessive antacids, as it can lead to an abnormal balance of stomach acid and potentially cause more harm than good. Typically, a recommended dose of antacids is one to two tablets, 30 minutes to 1 hour apart. Taking more than that can irritate your esophagus and worsen your symptoms. Additionally, relying solely on antacids to manage symptoms can mask underlying issues, rather than addressing the root cause.",
